apple:movie-start","objectID":"189EC917-69C0-496E-AF61-3D592930AECC"}],"automaticPlay":true,"hyperlinks":[],"accessibility":[{"text":"How a vector grows: Size and Capacity","targetRectangle":{"y":79,"x":99,"width":1522.4350013679266,"height":100.53440856933594}},{"text":"An array cannot be made longer. So what does a vector do when it is full and you push_back again?","targetRectangle":{"y":229.72444152832031,"x":111.69918060302734,"width":1626.6916406250007,"height":48}},{"text":"It gets a bigger block of memory, copies every element across and frees the old block. ","targetRectangle":{"y":341.91961669921875,"x":111.69918060302734,"width":801.82799999999997,"height":102}},{"text":"It asks for more room than it needs, so this does not happen every time.","targetRectangle":{"y":443.91961669921875,"x":111.69918060302734,"width":848.952,"height":100}},{"text":"size() is how many elements you have stored. capacity() is how many fit before the next move.","targetRectangle":{"y":543.91961669921875,"x":147.69918060302734,"width":841.10667187500007,"height":112.0159912109375}},{"text":"Without the reserve line the capacity doubles each time it runs out.","targetRectangle":{"y":655.93560791015625,"x":147.69918060302734,"width":821.51999999999987,"height":100}},{"text":"With reserve(8) it prints 1 of 8 to 5 of 8","targetRectangle":{"y":755.93560791015625,"x":147.69918060302734,"width":673.52315624999994,"height":63.00799560546875}},{"text":"Use reserve when you know roughly how many elements are coming.","targetRectangle":{"y":818.943603515625,"x":147.69918060302734,"width":801.31260937499985,"height":106.00799560546875}},{"text":"After a move, any pointer or iterator into the old block is no longer valid","targetRectangle":{"y":924.95159912109375,"x":147.69918060302734,"width":772.12800000000004,"height":84.99200439453125}}],"baseLayer":{"animations":[],"initialState":{"affineTransform":[1,0,0,1,0,0],"masksToBounds":false,"rotation":0,"scale":1,"position":{"pointX":960,"poin